markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Building Classifiers

Lesson 8 frames the problem through postmasters: will today's mail arrive late, or on time?

That's a classification problem, predicting a category, not a number.

## Lesson Vocabulary

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-2/building-classifiers-flip-cards.html"
    width="100%"
    height="280"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Building classifiers vocabulary flip cards: label, feature, classifier">
  </iframe>
</div>

## Predicting with One Feature

Students start with a single feature: snowfall. Here's the actual activity, five past days plotted on a number line by how much snow fell, each labeled Late or On Time, with "Today" placed somewhere among them.

<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 14pt; color: #111; max-width: 850px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; background-color: #fff;">

  <!-- Legend -->
  <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 28px; margin-bottom: 32px;">

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
    <span style="display: inline-block; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <strong>On Time</strong>
    </div>

  <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
      <span style="display: inline-block; width: 28px; height: 28px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 3px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <strong>Late</strong>
    </div>

   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;">
      <span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #000; color: #fff;" aria-hidden="true">?</span>
      <strong>Today</strong>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Snow continuum -->
  <div role="img" aria-label="Snow increases from left to right. Two on-time days appear toward less snow, followed by today, whose outcome is unknown. Three late days appear farther toward more snow." style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">

  <div style="flex: 0 0 52px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.3;">
      Less<br>Snow
    </div>

   <div style="position: relative; flex: 1; height: 48px;">

   <!-- Line -->
  <div style="position: absolute; left: 10px; right: 10px; top: 22px; height: 4px; background-color: #999;"></div>

  <!-- Arrowheads -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 0; top: 15px; width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 9px solid transparent; border-bottom: 9px solid transparent; border-right: 17px solid #999;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; right: 0; top: 15px; width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 9px solid transparent; border-bottom: 9px solid transparent; border-left: 17px solid #999;"></div>

   <!-- On-time days -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 15%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 23%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

  <!-- Today -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 40%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #000; color: #fff; font-size: 20pt;">?</div>

   <!-- Late days -->
  <div style="position: absolute; left: 49%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 40px; height: 40px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 4px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; left: 83%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 40px; height: 40px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 4px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; left: 92%; top: 4px; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 40px; height: 40px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 4px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

   </div>
  <div style="flex: 0 0 56px; font-weight: bold; line-height: 1.3;">
      More<br>Snow
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #4C42CF; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin-bottom: 10px;">Single Nearest Neighbor</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 6px;">1. Find the one past day closest to Today.</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 6px;">2. Borrow its label. Here, that's the Late day right next to Today.</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 14px; padding-left: 16px; color: #1F1976;">&rarr; Prediction: <strong>Late</strong></div>

  <div style="font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: #4C42CF; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; margin-bottom: 10px;">Three-Nearest-Neighbors</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 6px;">1. Find the three closest days instead of one.</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 6px;">2. Take a vote. Here, that's one Late day and two On Time days, a 2-to-1 vote.</div>
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 16px; color: #1F1976;">&rarr; Prediction: <strong>On Time</strong></div>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>&#128214; Nearest Neighbor:</strong> a simple way to classify, label new data using its nearest neighbor's label.</div>
</div>

## Adding a Second Feature

A single feature gets you only so far. Here's what the activity looks like once a second feature, visibility, enters the picture.

<div style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 500px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; background-color: #fff;">

  <div role="img" aria-label="Scatter plot with snowfall on the horizontal axis and visibility on the vertical axis. Purple filled and outlined circles generally rise as snowfall increases. A black circle with a question mark appears near the center." style="position: relative; width: 100%; height: 440px;">

<!-- Vertical axis label -->
  <div style="position: absolute; left: 0; top: 45%; transform: rotate(-90%); writing-mode: vertical-rl; rotate: 180deg; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">
      Visibility
    </div>

  <!-- Plot area -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 55px; right: 20px; top: 15px; bottom: 55px;">

    <!-- Vertical axis -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 0; top: 10px; bottom: 10px; width: 3px; background-color: #999;"></div>

   <!-- Vertical arrowheads -->
  <div style="position: absolute; left: -6px; top: 0; width: 0; height: 0; border-left: 8px solid transparent; border-right: 8px solid transparent; border-bottom: 15px solid #999;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; left: -6px; bottom: 0; width: 0; height: 0; border-left: 8px solid transparent; border-right: 8px solid transparent; border-top: 15px solid #999;"></div>

   <!-- Horizontal axis -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 10px; right: 10px; bottom: -8px; height: 3px; background-color: #999;"></div>

   <!-- Horizontal arrowheads -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: -14px; width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid transparent; border-bottom: 8px solid transparent; border-right: 15px solid #999;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: -14px; width: 0; height: 0; border-top: 8px solid transparent; border-bottom: 8px solid transparent; border-left: 15px solid #999;"></div>

   <!-- Filled purple points -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 15%; bottom: 10%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; left: 22%; bottom: 25%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

   <div style="position: absolute; left: 38%; bottom: 5%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 61%; bottom: 32%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 92%; bottom: 79%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #7050d8;"></div>

  <!-- Outlined purple points -->
  <div style="position: absolute; left: 47%; bottom: 72%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 3px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 66%; bottom: 77%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 3px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 63%; bottom: 58%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 3px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

  <div style="position: absolute; left: 84%; bottom: 63%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); width: 34px; height: 34px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 3px solid #7050d8; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #fff;"></div>

   <!-- Unknown point -->
   <div style="position: absolute; left: 56%; bottom: 45%; transform: translate(-50%, 50%); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; background-color: #000; color: #fff; font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold;">?</div>

  </div>
   <!-- Horizontal axis label -->
    <div style="position: absolute; left: 55px; right: 20px; bottom: 5px; text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">
      Snowfall
    </div>

  </div>
</div>

Each axis represents one feature, snowfall across the bottom, visibility up the side, so every past day becomes a point instead of a position on a line. 

"Nearest" now means closest on this plot, not just closest along one number line.

## How it looks in Python

To hold both of a day's feature values together in code, Python needs a structure built for exactly that: a dictionary.

<div style="border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; margin: 12px 0 16px 0; border: 1px solid #E4E2F8;">
  <div style="background-color: #1F1976; padding: 16px 20px; font-family: 'Consolas', 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 16px; color: #E4E2F8; line-height: 1.8;">
today = {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;"snowfall": 3,<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;"visibility": 7<br>
}
  </div>
</div>

- **Keys** on the left name each feature
- **Values** on the right hold its number
- both bundled together under one name, <code style="font-size:16px;">today</code>.

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><strong>&#128161; Teacher tip:</strong> students find the model's prediction two ways in Levels 1-3, visually on the plot (dashed lines connect "Today" to its nearest neighbors) and by reasoning about which label shows up most often among them. See the <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mZ08BFeNVtGWK6OuOoVH1OMZknUxiKTOlFgUKqee75o/edit?usp=sharing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold;">Nearest Neighbors Activity Guide</a> for the exact version students work through.</div>
</div>
 

In the next level, you'll try exactly this yourself, clicking to place "Today" on a two-feature plot and watching which past days it connects to.
MARKDOWN
